														Aye, I had a feeling this has been brewing for a while.  I support Aam's decision, and can completely understand what he's going through.<br />
<br />
I had a guild once, so I know how stressful it is.  You have to worry about everyone, and try to deal with every situation so as not to make 1 person too mad, which can start a chain reaction.  That takes a LOT of time from you, and therefore your personal life.  If you have 20 people in the guild, and 20 people want to just say &quot;hi&quot; in tells, or even in guild, you can be on forever just trying to keep morale up and not seem &quot;cliquey&quot;.  On top of that you have to &quot;babysit&quot; those who were poor choices brought into your guild, but handle it with &quot;kid gloves&quot; or else others may follow when you take what seems to be appropriate actions.  For that reason, I'd say that the guild would have been fine still if it had not been for the R/L stuff goin on (geez Aam, u had to get a job, didn't u ;).  I guess the perfect guild leader would be someone who didn't have a R/L or any R/L responsibilites, just on 24/7.<br />
<br />
Anyway, I have no hard feelings toward anyone, and just wanted Kattank to know that there are no hard feelings there.  Think of my previous post as just a loving, fatherly-type lecture.  You removed it, matter resolved.<br />
